{
  "id": "openclaw:core:skill_workshop",
  "source": "openclaw",
  "sourceName": "core",
  "name": "skill_workshop",
  "label": "Skill Workshop",
  "description": "Your learned skills: reusable procedures saved as <name>/SKILL.md that load in future sessions. Changes apply immediately, are versioned, and are shown to the user.\nActions: list | view name [file_path] [version] | create name content | patch name old_text new_text [file_path] | write_file name file_path content | remove_file name file_path | archive name (absorbed_into or reason) | restore name [version].\n- create: content is the full SKILL.md: frontmatter name (= name) and description (aim for ≤160 bytes, triggers first), then the procedure.\n- patch: replaces one exact, unique old_text; view first and copy the text exactly. Prefer patch over rewrites.\n- file_path: SKILL.md or files under references/, templates/, scripts/, assets/. remove_file deletes one of those support files; archive removes a whole skill.\n- reason: one short line saying what changed; shown to the user.\n- restore without version undoes the last change.\n\nSkill authoring standard:\n- A skill is a procedure, not memory: the method for one class of task this user repeats, so the next run starts from what worked instead of working it out again. Write ordered steps, each with the exact commands, tools, paths, and the check that shows it worked, then the user's standing preferences for the result. Facts about the user, people, or the world with no method attached belong in memory, not a skill.\n- Each rule is an imperative plus one clause of why, attached to the step it affects, stated as the behavior to produce. One rule per lesson; a repeated lesson sharpens the existing rule.\n- Fix the misleading sentence in place so the skill reads as current truth; leave out update notes, dates, ticket or PR ids, incident stories, and quoted user text.\n- Write plain instructions: every sentence should change what the agent does, so drop emphasis and praise.\n- description (aim for ≤160 bytes; keep existing triggers when editing): open with the trigger situations, one phrase per distinct case, then what the skill produces. Name the class of work, not today's task.\n- Keep in SKILL.md what every run needs; move what only some runs need into references/, templates/, or scripts/ and point to it from the step that needs it.",
  "input": "{ action: \"list\" | \"view\" | \"create\" | \"patch\" | \"write_file\" | \"remove_file\" | \"archive\" | \"restore\"; absorbed_into?: string; content?: string; file_path?: string; name?: string; new_text?: string; old_text?: string; reason?: string; version?: string }",
  "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "required": [
      "action"
    ],
    "properties": {
      "action": {
        "enum": [
          "list",
          "view",
          "create",
          "patch",
          "write_file",
          "remove_file",
          "archive",
          "restore"
        ],
        "type": "string"
      },
      "name": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Skill name (lowercase-hyphenated)."
      },
      "file_path": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "SKILL.md (default) or a file under references/, templates/, scripts/, assets/."
      },
      "content": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "create: full SKILL.md. write_file: full file content."
      },
      "old_text": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "patch: exact text to replace once."
      },
      "new_text": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "patch: replacement text."
      },
      "absorbed_into": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "archive: live skill that now covers this one."
      },
      "reason": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "One short line saying what changed and why; shown to the user."
      },
      "version": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "view/restore: version id; restore defaults to the newest."
      }
    },
    "additionalProperties": false
  }
}

